{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseStatusLineRawVersion\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">parseStatusLineRawVersion</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">limits</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Config.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Config\">Config</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Internal/Parsec/ByteArray.html#Std.Internal.Parsec.ByteArray.Parser\">Internal.Parsec.ByteArray.Parser</a> (<a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/Status.html#Std.Http.Status\">Status</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/Version.html#Std.Http.Version\">Version</a></span>)</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses a status line and returns the status code plus recognized HTTP version when available.\nConsumes and discards the reason phrase.\n\nRFC 9110 §2.5: a response with a higher minor version than HTTP/1.1 (`HTTP/1.2`) is processed as\nHTTP/1.1, the highest minor version this client implements.\n\nstatus-line = HTTP-version SP status-code SP [ reason-phrase ] CRLF","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseStatusLineRawVersion","kind":"def","line":617,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseStatusLineRawVersion","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.lean#L617-L629"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseStatusLine\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">parseStatusLine</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">limits</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Config.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Config\">Config</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Internal/Parsec/ByteArray.html#Std.Internal.Parsec.ByteArray.Parser\">Internal.Parsec.ByteArray.Parser</a> <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/Response.html#Std.Http.Response.Head\">Response.Head</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses a status line and returns a fully-typed `Response.Head`.\n`status-line = HTTP-version SP status-code SP [ reason-phrase ]`\nAccepts only HTTP/1.x, read as HTTP/1.1 for any minor version above 1. For parsing where the version\nmay be unrecognized and must be mapped to an error event, use `parseStatusLineRawVersion`.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseStatusLine","kind":"def","line":601,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseStatusLine","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.lean#L601-L615"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseTrailers\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">parseTrailers</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">limits</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Config.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Config\">Config</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Internal/Parsec/ByteArray.html#Std.Internal.Parsec.ByteArray.Parser\">Internal.Parsec.ByteArray.Parser</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> (<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>))</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses trailer headers after a chunked body and returns them as an array of name-value pairs.\n\nThis is exposed for callers that need the trailer values directly (e.g. clients). The\ninternal protocol machine parses the section one field at a time with `parseTrailerHeader`, and\ndiscards trailer values.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseTrailers","kind":"def","line":547,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseTrailers","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.lean#L547-L557"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseTrailerHeader\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">parseTrailerHeader</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">limits</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Config.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Config\">Config</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">strict</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a> := <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Internal/Parsec/ByteArray.html#Std.Internal.Parsec.ByteArray.Parser\">Internal.Parsec.ByteArray.Parser</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> (<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>))</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses a trailer header (used after a chunked body). Framing and routing fields\n(`isFramingTrailerField`) are always rejected, to prevent trailer injection attacks where a\ndownstream proxy might re-interpret them. With `strict`, every field forbidden in trailers is\nrejected; without it, the others are parsed and left for the caller to drop, since RFC 9110 §6.5.1\nasks recipients not to merge them rather than to reject a message that is otherwise complete.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseTrailerHeader","kind":"def","line":532,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseTrailerHeader","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.lean#L532-L545"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseChunkSizedData\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">parseChunkSizedData</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">size</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Internal/Parsec/ByteArray.html#Std.Internal.Parsec.ByteArray.Parser\">Internal.Parsec.ByteArray.Parser</a> <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.TakeResult\">TakeResult</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses fixed-size chunk data that can be incomplete.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseChunkSizedData","kind":"def","line":502,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseChunkSizedData","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.lean#L502-L508"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseFixedSizeData\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">parseFixedSizeData</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">size</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Internal/Parsec/ByteArray.html#Std.Internal.Parsec.ByteArray.Parser\">Internal.Parsec.ByteArray.Parser</a> <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.TakeResult\">TakeResult</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses fixed-size data that can be incomplete.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseFixedSizeData","kind":"def","line":491,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseFixedSizeData","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.lean#L491-L500"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Parser.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.parseChunkPartial\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">parseChunkPartial</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">limits</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Config.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Config\">Config</a>)</span